  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced capacity of labour administration for improved workplace compliance with emphasis on the informal sectors of the economy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The National Economic Development and Labour Council (NEDLAC) marks its 30 years in existence since the advent of democracy and to seeks to celebrate this milestone by sharing good practice experiences with similar formations on social dialogue in pursuit of social justice. Capacity issues, lack of trust and lack of access to information and resources, ineffectiveness in resolving disputes have weakened collective bargaining and its potential outcomes. The Commission for Conciliation, Mediation and Arbitration (CCMA) faces considerable strain from the high number of disputes referred to it. The labour administration in South Africa seeks to ensure the availability of relevant and timely labour market data to inform labour market policy through the establishment of a labour market information system. Linked to this is the need to align labour market statistical data with international statistical standards.
The strategy will focus on providing advisory support and facilitating linkages of NEDLAC with other similar formations for knowledge sharing on good practices in promoting social justice through social dialogue; capacity support on collective bargaining for Government and the Social Partners targeting sectors often susceptible to protracted and adversarial negotiations over working conditions; capacity support to dispute resolution institutions on the application of the ILO&#x2019;s diagnostic tool for self-assessing the effectiveness of dispute resolution institution; and technical and capacity support towards development and finalisation of a labour market information system</narrative>
  </description>
